{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"86372cbd4b76439edb9041576abb7dfc01d63bf176d0f30946645635dc750c60","digest":{"component_or_area":"bridge suggest-mapping command","key_entities":["rebar bridge suggest-mapping","mapping_probe.py","src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/mapping_config.py","src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/bridge.py","src/rebar/_cli/_bridge_commands.py","_bridge_suggest_mapping","_emit_nested_toml","_emit_config_toml","[tool.rebar.mapping]","issue_types","statuses","link_types","priority_map","hierarchy","status_map","create_defaults","jira.JIRA","tomllib","pyproject.toml"],"problem_keywords":["mapping configuration","jira probe","pre-population","vocabulary discovery","axis maps","read-only command"],"propositions":["A new read-only command `rebar bridge suggest-mapping <PROJECT>` probes a live Jira instance to discover vocabulary (issue types, statuses, link types, priorities) and emit a suggested `[tool.rebar.mapping]` configuration block","The probe uses only public high-level pycontribs `jira.JIRA` methods (issue_types, priorities, issue_link_types, statuses, createmeta, search_issues, transitions) with no private REST calls","When invoked with `--write`, the command atomically merges the suggested mapping into an existing `rebar.toml` or creates one, preserving existing flat `[jira]` and `[tracker]` sections while deep-merging under `[mapping.projects.<KEY>]` (existing keys win)","Transition hints are grounded in actual per-issue transitions from sample searches but flagged as best-effort/partial since Jira returns only transitions from each sample's current status","The serialization splits flat top-level config from nested `[mapping.*]` tables via an orchestrator `_emit_config_toml` that calls the existing `_emit_toml` for flat sections and a new `_emit_nested_toml` for nested mapping sub-tables","The command is fully read-only by default (no file writes, no issue creation/deletion) and uses offline fake-port testing with no live Jira credentials required"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787501585203177001,"uuid":"e6b54238-df56-459f-8be9-3fd966b2302c"}